$DIR/test.p:7:36: cannot convert x (variable of type float64) to enum type Color (only integers convert to an enum)
    Only integers convert to an enum, and a constant converts only if it is the
    value of a member. Anything else would make an enum value that is not a
    member. An enum type is not an integer type for this rule: a value of one
    enum type converts to another through its integer type, in the comma-ok
    form, v, ok := Shade(uint8(c)).
    (see "Enums" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.12)
    (run "pluto explain E2313" for a longer explanation)
